  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 100 AM CDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\nSaturday was another day of solid HI's topping out in the \n105-110 degree range, adding to our prolonged duration extreme \nheat. There were isolated higher totals up to 113 degrees, very\nsimilar to Friday. This was on target and will be so yet again \ntoday with very similar conditions to the past 2 days. Heat \nheadlines will thus remain in effect thru what will hopefully be\nits final day today.\n\nWhat changes after that is a noisier pattern manifest from\nfalling heights as the ridge shows some breaks and ultimately, a\ncouple frontal approaches and passages. The first such will be\ntonight into Monday, and there is a widespread swath of Marginal\nRisk severe with its presence, extending its entire latitudinal\nbounds from MO-VA. Marginal is good with marginal parameters in\nplace here, upper dynamics looking a tad better to our east,\nwhere a Slight risk exists. Temperatures and dew points fall off\nafter passage, but may not quite or fully enough to totally \npreclude another heat headline in our south for Monday. The dew\npoint drop off stalls a little down there in its decreasing \nwax, as upper 70s still hover on our southern borders in the \nlate PM, before dropping off in the evening. Fortunately, high \ntemps do cool back toward climo near 90F. As a result, at least\nat this writing, we're not prepared to extend, but it will be \nsomething to focus upon in the next 24 hours as peak HI's along\nour southern border flirt with Advisory criteria.\n\nAnother system takes shape by mid week, and it is messier in the\nmodels with its resolution, but for all practical purposes, it\nmakes incoming approach Wednesday with passage Wednesday night\ninto Thursday. Pops will spike during this time frame and a\nsharper punch of cooler/drier air is anticipated when its\npassage is completed. While no severe storms are highlighted \nnow, we suspect this may change as the pattern metamorphosis \noccurs and the mid week nears. On the plus side is the fruit \nthat'll bear, as we're looking at dew points returning to the \n60s by week's end, with Thursday-Friday highs solidly in the \nmid-upper 80s; a spectacular end to the week weather-wise, \nparticularly in comparison to the prior week of extreme heat. \nWe'll need to enjoy it while we can as both the 6-10 and 8-14 \nday outlooks return an Above normal temperature signal.",
